sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant NS_A as Notification Service (Node A)
    participant NS_B as Notification Service (Node B)
    participant Redis
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant Kafka

    %% Connection Phase
    User->>NS_A: STOMP CONNECT (with Validated JWT)
    NS_A->>Redis: SET user:123 -> Node_A (TTL: 1h)
    NS_A->>Redis: SADD instance:Node_A -> 123
    NS_A->>DB: Fetch PENDING notifications
    DB-->>NS_A: Return offline payload
    NS_A->>User: Flush offline notifications (if any)
    
    %% Event Consumption Phase
    Note over Kafka, NS_B: E.g., User Service emits KYC_SUCCESS
    Kafka->>NS_B: Consume NotificationEvent
    NS_B->>DB: Save Notification (Status: PENDING)
    NS_B->>Redis: GET user:123
    
    alt User is Online
        Redis-->>NS_B: Returns "Node_A"
        NS_B->>Redis: PUBLISH notify:Node_A {payload}
        Note over Redis, NS_A: Redis dynamically routes the message!
        Redis-->>NS_A: Message received on notify:Node_A
        NS_A->>DB: Update Status to DELIVERED (Atomic Claim)
        NS_A->>User: Push WebSocket STOMP Message (/queue/notifications)
    else User is Offline
        Redis-->>NS_B: Returns NULL
        Note over NS_B, DB: Notification remains safely in DB as PENDING.<br/>Will be delivered on next CONNECT.
    end
